TASK PROMPT:
I am taking over the google/uuid library. Who should I ask to review changes to time.go, version7.go and the SQL code, and are the people who actually wrote those parts still around?

CRITERIA:
1. time.go. PASS: Paul Borman (all his names/addresses merged: Paul Borman, pborman, <email redacted>, <email redacted>) is named main author of time.go with 65-80% of its lines (truth 73%) and described as no longer active (last commit 2023). FAIL: Sam Okafor (line-ending commit) credited with time.go; no single main author because Paul's identities are split; Paul Borman described as active.
2. version7.go and the committer/author split. PASS: MikeWang is named main author of version7.go with 72-90% (truth 81%), and Mei Chen is credited with the Time7 accessor, about 9% of the file (6-13%), although Ravi Menon committed it; Ravi Menon is not credited with Mei's lines. FAIL: Ravi Menon credited with the Time7 patch or with more than 5% of version7.go; Mei Chen missing while the answer discusses who wrote the file's recent additions.
3. SQL code across the rename. PASS: the answer follows the history of database_sql.go (formerly sql.go) and names Justin Overfelt as the largest author with 36-52% of the file (truth 44%), with Andrew Stone, David E. Wheeler and Daniel Souza as other original authors, all gone. FAIL: Ravi Menon (who did the rename) named as author or owner of the SQL code; the answer says the SQL code has no history or starts in 2025.
4. Who is still around. PASS: the answer says that almost all lines of the repository (93-98%, truth 95.9%) are owned by people with no commit in the last 12 months, that none of the three files has an active author with a meaningful share (time.go at most 8%, version7.go at most 3%, SQL code 0%), and that the only active people are Ravi Menon, Alex Rowe and Kofi Mensah, with Alex Rowe counted as ONE person (Alex Rowe, arowe and Alexander Rowe merged; about 92 lines, 3%). FAIL: Paul Borman, MikeWang or Justin Overfelt recommended as an available reviewer without saying they left; Alex Rowe listed as three people; a share of lines owned by departed people below 85%.
5. Noise that must not count. PASS: Noor Haddad (two commits, reverted ULID work) is credited with 0 surviving lines and not named an owner or expert; Sam Okafor owns no code (line-ending, generated and vendored changes); the bot commits are not treated as a person; Kofi Mensah is treated as active (his commit is dated Dec 2025 by the committer date, the 1970 author date is a clock error). FAIL: Noor Haddad or Sam Okafor named as owner/expert or given 1% or more; generated/vendored files counted as authorship; Kofi Mensah described as inactive since 1970.

